# Two files here have SHA-256 hashes published in the README, and the entire
# point of those hashes is that anyone can recompute them on their own machine.
# Git's autocrlf would rewrite line endings on a Windows checkout and break
# verification without changing a single visible character. Pin every text file
# to LF. The working tree is already LF everywhere, so this changes nothing
# today — it stops a future checkout from silently invalidating the hashes.
* text=auto eol=lf
